    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35329" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-pasco</span></b> , pāvi, pastum,
		3, v. n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to graze</i>, <i>pasture.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, § 95</span></i>
			Müll.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perpascor</span></b> , ci, 3, v. dep., <i>to lay waste</i>, <i>devastate</i>:
			fluvius perpascitur agros, Sev. Aetn. 489.—Hence, 
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perpastus</span></b> , a,
			um, P. a., <i>well fed</i>, <i>in good condition</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">canis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Phaedr. 3, 7, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
